  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: An anticyclone aloft will be centered\nover the South Central United States this afternoon. Monsoonal\nmoisture will remain in place in most of Northern and Central \nNevada, resulting in isolated to scattered thunderstorms this \nafternoon into this evening. There is a marginal risk of excessive\nrainfall in most of Northern and Central Nevada this afternoon \ninto this evening. Here are thunderstorm probabilities for select \nlocations in Eastern Nevada on Wednesday, July 22nd, 2026:\n\nEly - 55%\nLund - 53%\nGreat Basin National Park - 51%\nCurrie - 50%\nEureka - 46%\nWells - 45%\nRuby Lake - 44%\nSpring Creek - 42%\nElko - 40%\nJackpot - 35%\n\nThe aforementioned upper-level area of high pressure will expand \nnorthwestward Thursday through early next week. As a result, \nstorm chances will dwindle Thursday through Sunday, before ending \nby Monday of next week. A warming trend is expected Thursday and\nFriday. By Friday afternoon, high temperatures throughout Northern\nand Central Nevada will be around five degrees above normal for\nthis time of year. Heat-sensitvie ground in Northern Nevada will\nhave a moderate risk for heat-related illnesses Friday afternoon.\nA Heat Advisory may be required. Here are probabilities of triple\ndigit heat for select locations in Northern Nevada on Friday, July\n24th, 2026: \n\nWinnemucca - 95%\nBattle Mountain - 95%\nCrescent Valley - 95%\nWest Wendover - 65%\nCarlin - 65%\nElko - 55%\nMcDermitt - 45%\nOrovada - 30%\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence\nregarding very high atmospheric content today. High forecast\nconfidence in a few strong thunderstorms throughout Northern and \nCentral Nevada this afternoon into this evening. High forecast\nconfidence regarding a marginal risk of excessive rainfall in \nmost of Northern and Central Nevada this afternoon into this \nevening. High forecast confidence in a moderate risk of \nheat-related illnesses throughout Northern Nevada Friday \nafternoon. No deviations from the NBM model output.",
